F. Documents and declaration
•	Upload customer request / settlement form and other applicable supporting documents; enforce file type, file size and retention rules.
•	Require verification acknowledgement before submitting. Show required-documents checklist based on settlement type.
•	Actions: Cancel, Save Draft, Review & Submit. Draft must not post ledger entries.
Payout field-visibility rules
Payment method	Additional fields / constraints
Linked savings transfer	Display authorized linked account, beneficiary verification and transfer reference.
NEFT / RTGS	Collect validated beneficiary banking details and enforce configured limits.
Cheque	Capture payable party, clearing / cheque reference and bank-defined disbursement steps.
Cash	Only render if enabled by institution policy, amount thresholds and user permissions.

If the server returns no permitted payment methods, block the payout stage and display the supplied reason. Hide methods that are unavailable rather than allowing the user to select an invalid option.
4. FD and MIS — scheme-driven behavior
Use a single shared settlement component; drive visibility, labels, validation and calculation fields from backend scheme metadata. FD and MIS differ in how interest may have been accumulated or paid periodically.
Field / behavior	FD	MIS
Principal amount	Required	Required
Interest rate	Required	Required
Opening and maturity dates	Required	Required
Cumulative interest	When cumulative	Normally not cumulative
Periodic interest paid	If periodic-payout FD	Required when applicable
Last interest payout date	If periodic payouts	Show
Unpaid monthly installments	If scheme supports	Show if outstanding
Excess interest recovery	Conditional	Conditional
Premature penalty / deduction	Server-calculated	Server-calculated
Final net payable	Required	Required
Renewal / reinvestment	Only if supported	Only if supported

