Role and state behavior
State	Primary actions / UI
Draft	Edit, recalculate, save and cancel if permitted.
Calculated	Show quote ID and expiry; request review and submit.
Pending Approval	Maker sees status; checker sees Approve / Reject if authorized.
Rejected	Show reason; maker may correct and resubmit under workflow rules.
Approved	Display approval details; restrict post action to authorized role or service.
Posting / Payment Pending	Show progress and reference IDs; prevent duplicate posting.
Settled	Read-only record; settlement reference and downloadable / printable receipt.
Posting / Payment Failed	Display recoverable error and escalation/retry controlled by backend.

6. Validation, controls and error states
Scenario	Frontend requirement
Unknown deposit number	Show account-not-found message; preserve search inputs.
Closed or settled account	Disable a new settlement; provide existing settlement/receipt if permitted.
Premature closure	Apply eligibility and cut-off restrictions provided by backend.
Scheme disallows closure	Block submit and display user-readable denial reason.
Lien, freeze or legal hold	Block or route authorized exception approval per server response.
Outstanding loan against FD	Show linked liability and approved recovery/release requirements.
Joint holder instruction	Require operating-mode checks and signatures/authorizations.
Deceased depositor	Route to dedicated claim / deceased-account workflow when supported.
KYC/compliance restriction	Display restriction; prevent unauthorized override.
Calculation not available	Disable review, approval and settlement submission.
Quote expired / stale balance	Require recalculation and rerender new payable amount.
Payment limit exceeded	Show permitted method or required approval level.
Duplicate submission	Disable repeated clicks and use backend idempotency.
Approval rejected	Display rejection reason; route to correction if allowed.
Payment still pending	Never show final Settled state until backend confirmation.

Cross-cutting controls
•	Financial processing is server-authoritative: no local interest, TDS, penalty, waiver, outstanding-loan or rounding logic.
•	Role visibility enhances usability but is not authorization; enforce every protected operation on the server.
•	Use tamper-resistant quote/record IDs, concurrency checks and idempotency tokens for mutations.
•	Support error, empty, loading, stale quote and recoverable payment states. Never present a speculative success message.
•	Mask sensitive identifiers and avoid exposing unnecessary customer information in logs and UI telemetry.
7. Proposed API integration contract
The endpoints below are recommended interfaces, not verified existing application routes. Adapt naming, transport and permissions to the current backend without altering established business logic.
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/deposits/settlement-search	Find deposits using authorized filters.
GET	/api/deposits/{id}/settlement-context	Return customer, deposit, restrictions and scheme flags.
POST	/api/deposits/{id}/settlement-quote	Get authoritative line-item settlement calculation.
POST	/api/deposit-settlements	Create or save a draft request.
POST	/api/deposit-settlements/{id}/submit	Submit request to configured approval workflow.
POST	/api/deposit-settlements/{id}/approve	Authorize settlement via checker permission.
POST	/api/deposit-settlements/{id}/reject	Reject with explicit reason.
POST	/api/deposit-settlements/{id}/post	Perform authorized posting (if exposed as API).
GET	/api/deposit-settlements/{id}/receipt	Retrieve printable settlement receipt.

Frontend data contract — minimum expected properties
Domain	Suggested fields
Account context	depositId; accountNumberMasked; schemeCode; schemeName; customer; branch; principal; dates; status
Eligibility	eligible; permittedSettlementTypes; restrictions[]; requiredDocuments[]; paymentMethods[]
Scheme flags	interestPayoutFrequency; showMISPanel; renewalAllowed; configurableFields[]
Quote	quoteId; quoteExpiry; accountVersion; currency; lineItems[]; netPayable; warnings[]; blockingErrors[]
Settlement request	settlementId; requestStatus; settlementDate; reasonCode; remarks; beneficiary; documentIds[]
Audit / workflow	createdBy; submittedAt; approvedBy; approvedAt; rejectionReason; postingRef; paymentStatus

Integration rules
1.	Fetch an authoritative account context immediately after Select; clear old context when choosing another deposit.
2.	Recalculate whenever settlement date, type or another quote-critical parameter changes.
3.	Treat quote expiry, version mismatch and backend restrictions as hard submission blockers.
4.	Use exactly one request submission path with idempotency protection and explicit in-flight loading state.
5.	Refetch state after approval, posting and receipt operations; do not infer workflow transitions locally.
