Responsive layout
Viewport	Layout behavior
Desktop (>= 1024 px)	Two columns, approx. 7/5 or 8/4 ratio; keep settlement summary visible while scrolling if practical.
Tablet (768–1023 px)	Stack some panels or retain compact columns; do not compress monetary rows into unreadable cells.
Mobile (< 768 px)	Single column; search filters stack; results use horizontal scroll or compact record cards; sticky action footer if appropriate.

Accessibility and interaction standards
•	Associate labels and helper text with every control. Clearly identify required inputs and invalid fields.
•	Ensure keyboard navigation, focus-visible outlines, meaningful status text and accessible dialogs.
•	Do not communicate approval, failure or eligibility with color alone.
•	Use Indian numbering convention and two decimal places for INR; keep monetary alignment consistent.
•	Read-only financial and account fields must be clearly distinct from editable inputs.
•	Show skeletons on account load, spinners on quote and posting operations, and retry actions for safe requests.
•	On Leave page / Change Account, warn about unsaved edits and clear stale quote state.
